#: ../../security-manual/vulnerabilities.rst:377
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The ``openembedded-core/scripts/contrib/improve_kernel_cve_report.py`` "
"script leverages CVE kernel metadata and the "
":term:`SPDX_INCLUDE_COMPILED_SOURCES` variable to update an output "
"``.sbom-cve-check.yocto.json`` report file (see section :ref:`security-"
"manual/vulnerabilities:Vulnerability check at build time` for details on "
"these report files). It reduces CVE false positives by 70%-80% and "
"provide detailed responses for all kernel-related CVEs by analyzing the "
"files used to build the kernel. The script is decoupled from the build "
"and can be run outside of the :term:`BitBake` environment."
msgstr "Lo script ``openembedded-core/scripts/contrib/improve_kernel_cve_report.py`` sfrutta i metadati CVE del kernel e la variabile :term:`SPDX_INCLUDE_COMPILED_SOURCES` per aggiornare un file di report di output ``.sbom-cve-check.yocto.json`` (vedere la sezione :ref:`security-manual/vulnerabilities:Vulnerability check at build time` per i dettagli su questi file di report). Riduce i falsi positivi CVE del 70%-80% e fornisce risposte dettagliate per tutte le CVE relative al kernel analizzando i file utilizzati per la compilazione del kernel. Lo script è indipendente dal processo di compilazione e può essere eseguito al di fuori dell'ambiente :term:`BitBake`."

#: ../../security-manual/vulnerabilities.rst:386
msgid ""
